0.55: Deep code review pass (vs official _example_clock, antonclk, widbat, Espruino Discussion #1800). Clears + charging-icon zone now anchored to appRect (appBottom = appTop + appH; icon zone x154-176, y appBottom-18..appBottom-1), appTop/appH cached after setUI via cacheAppRect() — no more hardcoded 157/158/175. Step count clamped at 99999 ("99999 steps" = 132px, ends x153) so 6+ digits can't invade the icon zone. y advance moved out of each section's try/catch so layout always progresses. Gap count fixed: gap*(hasWeather?5:4) instead of gap*5 (was 8px over-tall without weather, shifting content up 4px). Charging icon redrawn at end of every draw() so it can't go stale. onStep read throttled to 1/s (getHealthStatus on every step event was storage churn). No visual change at default geometry
0.54: Added g.reset() as the first line of draw() — resets the shared graphics state (color/font/align/clip) to theme defaults before drawing, so state mutated by widgets or other apps (e.g. widbat leaving bgColor poisoned at <20% battery) can't leak into minwatch's rendering. Structural guard for the whole widget-state-pollution class; no visual change vs 0.53 (verified via minwatchreset test build 0.0.1)
0.53: Re-applied event-driven charging icon (drawn only at init and on charging events, not every minute). Icon zone (x154-176, y158-175) excluded from the per-minute clear so the icon persists; content clear capped at y157 plus a strip clear x0-154/y158-175 so the steps row (y~156-172 with weather) clears each minute when step-count width changes (4→5 digits) or weather appears/disappears. Verified via minwatchtest builds 0.0.1-0.0.4
0.52: Red background across the whole content area after a minute change. Root cause: the default widbat widget calls g.setBgColor("#f00") when battery is <20% and never restores; the next minute's content-area clearRect then filled the panel red. Fix: g.setBgColor(g.theme.bg) set explicitly before the content-area clear, so red persists only within the widget's own region
0.51: Keep the minute-aligned redraw running while the LCD is off — since v0.31 onLcdPower(false) cleared drawTimeout, so the panel time went stale during idle and only refreshed on wake. The redraw now fires exactly at each minute change (queueDraw = 60000 - Date.now()%60000) even with the display blanked, so the shown minute always matches the real minute. Wake still triggers an immediate full redraw. Negligible battery cost (one draw/min)
0.50: Full content-area clear + redraw every minute, immediate full redraw on wake (lcdPower on). Final root cause of the persistent dark-theme 'white background at first redraw': NOT a draw bug — Bangle.js 2 firmware powers the LCD off after ~20s idle (DEFAULT_LCD_POWER_TIMEOUT 20000), and the LPM013M126 then shows its natural white state. Watchface renders correctly on load and on every wake. Full redraw per minute retained (cheap ~10KB SPI/min, removes the old bar); earlier partial-flush/decay theories ruled out by on-device tests
0.49: Full content-area clear + redraw on first scheduled draw only — the bar artifact is a partial-band LCD flush after a ~60s static period; full-area flushes are immune. Partial redraws resume from minute 2. Also reset prevSegments on full clear (latent blank-bar bug)
0.48: Removed redundant full-width clearRect before time drawString — drawString(...,true) already clears its own cell box; full-width band op is the suspected cause of the pre-existing debug bar artifact on the first minute re-draw
0.47: Isolate step 1 — v0.45 base + battery segment tracking (prevSegments) only, date caching removed. v0.46 confirmed v0.40's changes blank the content at minute update; testing which of the two sub-changes breaks it
0.46: Bisect step 3 — v0.37 base + v0.40's date caching (cachedDay/cachedDateStr) and battery segment tracking (prevSegments). v0.45 confirmed charging-icon change is safe
0.45: Bisect step 2 — v0.37 base + v0.39's charging-icon change (drawChargingIcon at init only, removed from draw()). BLE interval dropped: v0.44 confirmed NRF.setConnectionInterval(4000) at init is the crash trigger
0.44: Bisect step 1 — v0.37 base + v0.38's only change: NRF.setConnectionInterval(4000). v0.37 confirmed working on-device; re-adding one change at a time to find the crash trigger
0.37: Event-driven step counting — switched from per-minute polling to Bangle.on('step') handler, zero overhead when idle
0.36: Fixed step counter — switched from Bangle.getStepCount() (never resets) to Bangle.getHealthStatus("day").steps (resets at midnight), added ||0 fallback, removed setPollInterval(800) (firmware auto-throttles correctly)
0.35: Cached font heights at init, guarded clearRect against missing Bangle.appRect
0.34: Weather redraw skipped when data unchanged (saves ~59 redraws/hour)
0.33: Fixed CW display (replaced unsupported Date.UTC/getUTCDay with local time), fixed layout alignment (appTop >= 24 for widget bar)
0.32: Fixed dark theme rendering — replaced hardcoded g.setColor(0) with g.theme.fg/g.theme.bg
0.31: Fix layout overflow (totalH inflation, +16 offset), lcdPower handler with queueDraw on power-on, single E.getBattery call, prevHadWeather early update, clearRect bounded to appRect, redraw:draw in setUI, setPollInterval guard, w.temp typeof validation
0.30: Removed redundant g.reset() in draw (all state set explicitly after), added w.code existence check before drawWeatherIcon
0.29: Re-added Bangle.setPollInterval(800) — reduces accelerometer from 0.3mA to 0.15mA (v0.22 removal was about JS events, not pedometer)
0.28: Reduced weather cache TTL from 5min to 60min — weather data updates hourly anyway, saves unnecessary Storage.read calls
0.27: Per-element clear + selective redraw — no full-screen clear unless layout shifts (weather appear/disappear). Saves ~65% SPI pixels on typical minute
0.26: Power optimization — content-area-only clear (saves ~10.5% SPI pixels vs full Bangle.appRect clear)
0.25: Reverted draw() to v0.23 proven structure — fresh per-draw computation of appTop/appH/th/sh, per-element try/catch for fault isolation, g.reset() inside try after layout calc; kept init improvements (deferred drawWidgets, listener cleanup)
0.24.1: Fixed v0.24 regression — moved appRect/font height caching after Bangle.loadWidgets() (loadWidgets may modify appRect, causing stale cached values)
0.24: Code review optimizations — cached appRect/font heights at init, removed inner try/catch blocks, moved g.reset() before try, deferred drawWidgets with setTimeout (antonclk pattern)
